### TITLE ###
PlaceholderShowsWhileEmptyAndVanishesOnTyping
### DESCRIPTION ###
The placeholder is a prompt for what to type, not a value, so it must not
survive the first keystroke.
### PROMPT ###
>
### PLACEHOLDER ###
name here
### KEYS ###
"x"
enter
### VALUE ###
x
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
>█name here
--- frame 1 (x) ---
>x█
--- frame 2 (enter) ---
>x

### TITLE ###
NarrowWidthClampsTheDisplayNotTheValue
### DESCRIPTION ###
A field narrower than its contents truncates what it draws, and VALUE shows the
full string still comes back. Clamping the value instead would silently discard
what the user typed.
### PROMPT ###
>
### WIDTH ###
6
### KEYS ###
"abcdefghij"
enter
### VALUE ###
abcdefghij
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
>█
--- frame 1 (a) ---
>a█
--- frame 2 (b) ---
>ab█
--- frame 3 (c) ---
>abc█
--- frame 4 (d) ---
>abcd█
--- frame 5 (e) ---
>…cde█
--- frame 6 (f) ---
>…def█
--- frame 7 (g) ---
>…efg█
--- frame 8 (h) ---
>…fgh█
--- frame 9 (i) ---
>…ghi█
--- frame 10 (j) ---
>…hij█
--- frame 11 (enter) ---
>abcdefghij
